From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NanoPi K1 Plus OpenWrt project <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rtl8189es: v3 delayed inert — sleep 5 before exit

Applies on top of 007-stabilize-k1-plus-rtl8189es-radio.patch.

Hypothesis: 50_rtl-wifi (uci-defaults) executes during early boot, before
netifd has finished first-boot br-lan initialization. Any activity from the
rtl8189es package script at that point can race the network setup; on the
K1 Plus this showed up as eth0 dying after a switch to DHCP.

Delay the script 5 seconds so the network stack settles first. The script
still does nothing else (inert), so no new driver load or radio mutation is
introduced — the only new variable is timing.

---
 package/kernel/rtl8189es/files/50_rtl-wifi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/package/kernel/rtl8189es/files/50_rtl-wifi b/package/kernel/rtl8189es/files/50_rtl-wifi
index 2222222..3333333 100644
--- a/package/kernel/rtl8189es/files/50_rtl-wifi
+++ b/package/kernel/rtl8189es/files/50_rtl-wifi
@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
 #!/bin/sh
+# Delay: let netifd finish first-boot br-lan initialization
+sleep 5
 # NanoPi K1 Plus relies on the shared wifi generator instead of package-local
 # rtl8189es boot mutations.
 exit 0
